## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of SageMaker for anomaly detection, focusing on real-time latency requirements, data residency constraints, and phased deployment strategies using canary releases.

## Key Concepts
- Anomaly detection models (Isolation Forest, autoencoders)
- Time-series feature engineering (rolling windows)
- Endpoint configuration and autoscaling (min/max instances, latency targets)
- Monitoring and drift detection (SageMaker Clarify, CloudWatch)
- Cost optimization and regional data compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
{
  "TrainingJobName": "anomaly-detection-train",
  "AlgorithmSpecification": { 
    "TrainingImage": "<isolation-forest-image>", 
    "TrainingInputMode": "File" 
  },
  "InputDataConfig": [{
    "ChannelName": "training",
    "DataSource": {
      "S3DataSource": {
        "S3DataType": "S3Prefix",
        "S3Uri": "s3://training-data/login-patterns/"
      }
    }
  }]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical, production-ready approach to multi-tenant inference, with per-tenant routing, canary risk controls, and drift/latency monitoring within a VPC-bound data-residency model.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Endpoint variants and traffic weighting
- Per-tenant routing and isolation
- PrivateLink data lake access
- Canary rollout and rollback triggers
- Drift and latency monitoring, autoscaling, and cost control

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo AWS SDK snippet: adjust variant weights per-tenant
const params = {
  EndpointName: 'inference-endpoint',
  DesiredWeights: {
    'VariantA': 0.5,
    'VariantB': 0.5
  }
};
sagemaker.updateEndpointWeightsAndCapacities(params, cb);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle tenant onboarding/offboarding without impacting others?
- What metrics would you surface in dashboards to verify drift controls remain effective?
